       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The current FDA label for prescription ibuprofen doesn't support it.\n\n- The labeled maximum is **3,200 mg/day**, and a single dose shouldn't exceed 800 mg. The OTC limit is lower, at 1,200 mg/day.\n- 1600 mg four times daily is **6,400 mg/day**, twice the labeled maximum.\n\nIf you have a label or reference that says otherwise, please send it and I'll look at it again. I'd be surprised if there is one. This order would be off-label, and I'm not aware of any evidence that doses this high work better. They do raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you want to go above the label for a specific reason, that decision should go through the attending and pharmacy under your institution's process. I'm happy to enter an order once that's done. Which of the doses above would you like?"
